"use strict";(self.webpackChunkdatabricks_monolith=self.webpackChunkdatabricks_monolith||[]).push([[28079],{650460:e=>{e.exports="# ETL Pipeline Modernization\n\nSnowflake pipeline objects (Snowpipe, Stream, Task, Dynamic Table) → Databricks Workflows, Delta Live Tables, Auto Loader, Change Data Feed.\n\n## Output format guidance\n\nChoose the output format based on the source artifact and the user's target:\n\n| Source                                       | Recommended output                                                                  |\n| -------------------------------------------- | ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| Snowflake SQL statements / stored procedures | DBSQL code blocks (the normal migration output)                                     |\n| Snowflake TASK DAG (multi-task, scheduled)   | Prose mapping of tasks → Workflow tasks / DLT pipeline, plus converted SQL per step |\n| Snowpipe + STAGE + STREAM                    | DLT streaming table or Auto Loader + COPY INTO, plus pipeline configuration         |\n| Snowflake DYNAMIC TABLE                      | DLT streaming table / materialized view in a DLT pipeline                           |\n\nIf the user has not specified their target (Workflows vs DLT), ask before producing output — the two paths produce different artifacts.\n\n## Snowflake pipeline objects → DBSQL mapping\n\n| Snowflake                                                                 | DBSQL equivalent                                                                                                                        | Notes                                                                                                                |\n| ------------------------------------------------------------------------- | --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- | -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `CREATE STAGE my_stage URL = 's3://...'`                                  | Unity Catalog **Managed Volume** (internal) or **External Volume** backed by a UC External Location + Storage Credential (user-managed) | Choose based on whether the source stage was internal (Snowflake-managed) or external (pointed at customer storage). |\n| `CREATE FILE FORMAT my_fmt TYPE = PARQUET`                                | No object equivalent                                                                                                                    | Specify format inline in `COPY INTO` via `FILEFORMAT = PARQUET`                                                      |\n| `COPY INTO t FROM @my_stage FILE_FORMAT = my_fmt`                         | `COPY INTO my_catalog.my_schema.t FROM 's3://...' FILEFORMAT = PARQUET`                                                                 | Both dialects have `COPY INTO` with similar syntax                                                                   |\n| `CREATE PIPE my_pipe AS COPY INTO t FROM @stage` (Snowpipe)               | Auto Loader (`cloud_files`) or DLT streaming table                                                                                      | Continuous ingestion                                                                                                 |\n| `CREATE STREAM s ON TABLE t` (CDC)                                        | Delta Change Data Feed + streaming read                                                                                                 | Enable CDF on target table                                                                                           |\n| `CREATE TASK t ... AS <sql>` (scheduled)                                  | Databricks Workflow task or DLT pipeline                                                                                                |                                                                                                                      |\n| `CREATE TASK ... AFTER parent_task` (DAG)                                 | Workflow task with `depends_on`                                                                                                         |                                                                                                                      |\n| `CREATE DYNAMIC TABLE ...` (declarative pipelines)                        | DLT streaming table / materialized view                                                                                                 |                                                                                                                      |\n| `ALTER PIPE my_pipe REFRESH`                                              | Trigger Auto Loader run / refresh DLT pipeline                                                                                          | Platform-level action                                                                                                |\n| External functions (`CREATE EXTERNAL FUNCTION ... API_INTEGRATION = ...`) | Databricks notebook / Python UDF calling the external API                                                                               | Or Databricks AI Gateway for LLM calls                                                                               |\n\n## Detailed examples\n\n### COPY INTO (bulk load)\n\n**DBSQL `COPY INTO` requires the target Delta table to already exist.** Unlike Snowflake, where the engine may load into a table that does not exist yet, DBSQL's documented contract is to load into \"an existing Delta table\" — there is no implicit create. If the Snowflake source did not include a pre-load `CREATE TABLE`, the translation must add one (or assume the table is created elsewhere in the migrated codebase).\n\nThe schema may be either declared up front (recommended for production) or inferred at load with `CREATE TABLE name` (no column list) + `COPY_OPTIONS ('mergeSchema' = 'true')` on DBR 11.3 LTS+. Pick declared-up-front for stable contracts and explicit casts; pick inferred for prototyping or when source schemas evolve frequently.\n\nTwo forms to choose between:\n\n- **Form A (direct path)** — load files straight into the table. Columns match position/name. No transformations.\n- **Form B (`FROM (SELECT ... FROM 'path')` subquery)** — select, rename, cast, or filter source columns before load. Required when (a) the source files have more or differently typed columns than the destination, (b) the migration needs explicit casts (e.g. `TRY_CAST(col AS DECIMAL(28,8))`), or (c) the Snowflake source used a `TRANSFORM` clause or column ordinals in `COPY INTO`. Restriction: only global aggregates are allowed; no `GROUP BY`.\n\n```sql\n-- Snowflake\nCREATE STAGE my_stage URL = 's3://mybucket/data/' STORAGE_INTEGRATION = my_int;\nCREATE FILE FORMAT my_parquet TYPE = PARQUET;\nCOPY INTO my_db.my_schema.my_table\nFROM @my_stage\nFILE_FORMAT = my_parquet\nPATTERN = '.*\\\\.parquet';\n\n-- DBSQL — target table must already exist with declared columns\n-- (UC external location set up once outside the SQL):\n--   CREATE EXTERNAL LOCATION my_loc URL 's3://mybucket/data/' WITH (STORAGE CREDENTIAL my_cred);\nCREATE TABLE IF NOT EXISTS my_catalog.my_schema.my_table (\n  ord_id BIGINT,\n  ord_dt DATE,\n  ord_amt DECIMAL(28, 8)\n);\n\n-- Form A — direct load when source columns map 1:1 to the table.\nCOPY INTO my_catalog.my_schema.my_table\nFROM 's3://mybucket/data/'\nFILEFORMAT = PARQUET\nPATTERN = '*.parquet';\n\n-- Form B — subquery for column projection, rename, or cast.\n-- Headerless CSV: reference columns positionally as _c0, _c1, _c2, ...\nCOPY INTO my_catalog.my_schema.my_table\nFROM (\n  SELECT\n    _c0::BIGINT                              AS ord_id,\n    TO_DATE(_c1, 'yyyy-MM-dd')               AS ord_dt,\n    TRY_CAST(_c2 AS DECIMAL(28, 8))          AS ord_amt\n  FROM 's3://mybucket/data/'\n)\nFILEFORMAT = CSV\nPATTERN = '*.csv';\n\n-- Form B with a header row: reference columns by header name.\nCOPY INTO my_catalog.my_schema.my_table\nFROM (\n  SELECT\n    order_id::BIGINT                         AS ord_id,\n    TO_DATE(order_date, 'yyyy-MM-dd')        AS ord_dt,\n    TRY_CAST(order_amount AS DECIMAL(28, 8)) AS ord_amt\n  FROM 's3://mybucket/data/'\n)\nFILEFORMAT = CSV\nPATTERN = '*.csv'\nFORMAT_OPTIONS ('header' = 'true');\n```\n\n**Header vs no header.** `_c0`, `_c1`, … positional refs only work when the CSV has no header row. If `FORMAT_OPTIONS ('header' = 'true')` is set, columns must be referenced by their header name — mixing the two silently picks up wrong columns.\n\n**`PATTERN` semantics differ**: Snowflake `PATTERN` is a **regex**; DBSQL `PATTERN` is a **glob**. Do not copy the expression verbatim — translate deliberately. A Snowflake regex `'orders_.*_v2\\.parquet'` becomes the glob `'orders_*_v2.parquet'`; the dot is a literal in globs but a metacharacter in regex.\n\n**Schema evolution.** If the Snowflake source allowed new columns to appear in files, add `COPY_OPTIONS ('mergeSchema' = 'true')`. This handles additive evolution — new columns from incoming files are added to the target. If the migration also needs to rename or drop columns later, additionally set `ALTER TABLE … SET TBLPROPERTIES ('delta.columnMapping.mode' = 'name')` — column mapping mode is required for rename/drop, not for additive `mergeSchema`.\n\n> For full `COPY INTO`, external location, and volume syntax, load `skills/writing-sql/foreign-tables.md`.\n\n### Snowpipe → Auto Loader / DLT\n\nSnowpipe is always-on auto-ingestion from a stage. DBSQL equivalents:\n\n- **DLT streaming table** — declarative, SQL-first path:\n  ```sql\n  -- In a DLT SQL pipeline notebook:\n  CREATE OR REFRESH STREAMING TABLE my_catalog.my_schema.my_table\n  AS SELECT * FROM STREAM read_files('s3://mybucket/data/', format => 'parquet');\n  ```\n- **Auto Loader in a notebook** — Python-first, more flexible, deployed via a Workflow task:\n  ```python\n  # Python cell in a notebook task\n  (spark.readStream\n    .format(\"cloudFiles\")\n    .option(\"cloudFiles.format\", \"parquet\")\n    .load(\"s3://mybucket/data/\")\n    .writeStream\n    .option(\"checkpointLocation\", \"/tmp/ckpt/my_table\")\n    .toTable(\"my_catalog.my_schema.my_table\"))\n  ```\n\n### STREAM (change data capture)\n\n```sql\n-- Snowflake stream on a table\nCREATE STREAM s ON TABLE my_table;\n-- Consume only true inserts (excluding the INSERT half of updates).\n-- METADATA$ACTION = 'INSERT' alone also captures the post-image of updates.\nSELECT * FROM s WHERE METADATA$ACTION = 'INSERT' AND METADATA$ISUPDATE = FALSE;\n\n-- DBSQL Change Data Feed\nALTER TABLE my_catalog.my_schema.my_table\nSET TBLPROPERTIES (delta.enableChangeDataFeed = true);\n\nSELECT *\nFROM table_changes('my_catalog.my_schema.my_table', '2024-01-01', current_timestamp())\nWHERE _change_type = 'insert';\n```\n\n**Metadata column mapping:**\n\n| Snowflake stream                             | DBSQL `table_changes()`                                                               |\n| -------------------------------------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `METADATA$ACTION` = `'INSERT'` or `'DELETE'` | `_change_type` = `'insert'`, `'delete'`, `'update_preimage'`, or `'update_postimage'` |\n| `METADATA$ISUPDATE` = TRUE                   | Represented as a paired `update_preimage` + `update_postimage` row                    |\n| `METADATA$ROW_ID`                            | No equivalent                                                                         |\n\n**Update representation differs**: Snowflake streams emit a DELETE + INSERT pair when `METADATA$ISUPDATE = TRUE`. DBSQL emits explicit `update_preimage` + `update_postimage` rows. Downstream logic that branches on `METADATA$ISUPDATE` needs to be rewritten to pair `update_preimage` with `update_postimage` by key.\n\n### TASK (scheduled SQL)\n\nSnowflake tasks form a DAG of scheduled SQL steps. Migrate to a Databricks Workflow.\n\n```sql\n-- Snowflake task DAG\nCREATE TASK daily_load_orders\n  WAREHOUSE = my_wh\n  SCHEDULE = 'USING CRON 0 3 * * * UTC'\nAS\n  MERGE INTO orders_target t USING orders_staging s ON t.id = s.id\n  WHEN MATCHED THEN UPDATE SET * WHEN NOT MATCHED THEN INSERT *;\n\nCREATE TASK post_load_audit\n  AFTER daily_load_orders\nAS\n  INSERT INTO audit_log\n  SELECT 'orders', count(*), current_timestamp FROM orders_target;\n\nALTER TASK daily_load_orders RESUME;\nALTER TASK post_load_audit RESUME;\n```\n\nDatabricks Workflow mapping (prose + per-step SQL):\n\n```\nDatabricks Workflow: daily_orders_pipeline\n├── Task 1: merge_orders (SQL task)\n│   SQL: MERGE INTO my_catalog.my_schema.orders_target t\n│        USING my_catalog.my_schema.orders_staging s ON t.id = s.id\n│        WHEN MATCHED THEN UPDATE SET *\n│        WHEN NOT MATCHED THEN INSERT *;\n│\n├── Task 2: audit_log (SQL task, depends_on = merge_orders)\n│   SQL: INSERT INTO my_catalog.my_schema.audit_log\n│        SELECT 'orders', count(*), current_timestamp\n│        FROM my_catalog.my_schema.orders_target;\n│\n└── Schedule: cron \"0 3 * * ?\" UTC\n```\n\nSnowflake `WAREHOUSE = my_wh` → DBSQL SQL warehouse configured at the task level (outside SQL). Drop the clause from the SQL body.\n\n### Dynamic tables → DLT\n\nSnowflake Dynamic Tables are declarative pipelines (target lag, auto-refresh). DLT (Delta Live Tables) is the DBSQL analog. Choose the target object based on the source:\n\n- **Append-only sources with low-lag requirements** → DLT `STREAMING TABLE` (consumes a streaming source). Use pipeline `Continuous` mode to approximate Snowflake's low `TARGET_LAG`.\n- **Full-recomputation or aggregation queries** → DLT `MATERIALIZED VIEW`. Refreshes happen on each pipeline trigger regardless of pipeline mode — Continuous mode does NOT make an MV continuously-refreshed. Approximate `TARGET_LAG` by scheduling the triggered pipeline at the desired cadence.\n\n```sql\n-- Snowflake Dynamic Table\nCREATE DYNAMIC TABLE sales_agg\nTARGET_LAG = '5 minutes'\nWAREHOUSE = my_wh\nAS\nSELECT region, SUM(amount) AS total FROM orders GROUP BY region;\n\n-- DBSQL: DLT materialized view (or streaming table) in a DLT pipeline\n-- Inside a DLT SQL notebook:\nCREATE OR REFRESH MATERIALIZED VIEW sales_agg AS\nSELECT region, SUM(amount) AS total FROM my_catalog.my_schema.orders GROUP BY region;\n-- Pipeline configured with Triggered or Continuous mode; target lag\n-- is approximated via pipeline schedule + streaming.\n```\n\nDLT pipelines created after 2025-02-05 use **direct publishing** — reference other pipeline tables with their full Unity Catalog name (`catalog.schema.table`). The legacy `LIVE.` virtual schema is still accepted on older pipelines but should not be used for new work. `TARGET_LAG` does not translate directly — choose between Triggered mode (run on schedule) and Continuous mode (always-on) based on the source lag target.\n\n## Batch ETL pattern\n\n**Watermark table** — tracks the last-processed timestamp so each run only processes new rows. Create it once before the first pipeline run:\n\n```sql\nCREATE TABLE IF NOT EXISTS my_catalog.staging.watermark (\n    table_name STRING,\n    last_updated_at TIMESTAMP\n);\nINSERT INTO my_catalog.staging.watermark VALUES ('orders', TIMESTAMP '1970-01-01 00:00:00');\n```\n\n**Incremental load + MERGE** — standard pattern for each pipeline run. Use `CREATE OR REPLACE TABLE` instead of `TRUNCATE` + `INSERT` so the staging replacement is a single atomic transaction; a mid-flight task failure can't leave the staging table empty while the watermark hasn't advanced.\n\n```sql\nCREATE OR REPLACE TABLE my_catalog.staging.orders AS\nSELECT * FROM source_catalog.source_schema.orders\nWHERE updated_at > (SELECT last_updated_at FROM my_catalog.staging.watermark WHERE table_name = 'orders');\n\nMERGE INTO my_catalog.target_schema.orders t\nUSING my_catalog.staging.orders s ON t.order_id = s.order_id\nWHEN MATCHED THEN UPDATE SET *\nWHEN NOT MATCHED THEN INSERT *;\n\nUPDATE my_catalog.staging.watermark\nSET last_updated_at = (SELECT MAX(updated_at) FROM my_catalog.staging.orders)\nWHERE table_name = 'orders';\n```\n\nAcross the three statements each one is individually atomic in Delta, but the sequence is not — if the pipeline dies between MERGE and the watermark UPDATE, the next run re-merges rows already applied. The MERGE is idempotent on `order_id` so this is safe for simple upserts; SCD-2 or keys that include a timestamp need an additional idempotency guard.\n"}}]);
